IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 36 and 37: labour disputes; prison inmates and persons outside
-- Canada. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Seat: the claimant.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). Both sections take away the claimant's claim to benefits for a time (the Commission has a
-- privilege not to pay; the claimant has a no-right). Section 36(4) is the claimant's immunity if they prove they are
-- not involved in the dispute; s 36(3) suspends the disentitlement, restoring the claim.
--
-- Whether a dispute is a "labour dispute" is s 2(1) (the keel's `s 2(1) labour dispute`); the caller feeds this module
-- its result. When a work stoppage ends is reg 53 (out of range: Regulations s 53, piece er3); how many days of
-- disentitlement a part-time claimant has in a week is reg 52 (out of range: Regulations s 52, piece er3); which
-- inmates and which absences from Canada are excepted is regs 54 and 55 (out of range: Regulations ss 54 and 55,
-- piece er3). Each is an input here, never worked out.
-- Section 36(2) is a regulation-making power (inert machinery: see the coverage table).

§ `Section 36 - labour disputes`

-- (5): "If separate branches of work that are commonly carried on as separate businesses in separate premises are carried
-- on in separate departments on the same premises, each department is, for the purpose of this section, a separate
-- factory or workshop." A deeming rule: JUST TRUE when it applies, NOTHING when it does not.
-- src:821 | Separate branches of work
-- src:822 | (5) If separate branches of work that are commonly carried on as separate businesses in separate premises are carried on in separate departments on the same premises, each department is, for the purpose of this section, a separate factory or workshop.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 36(5) (src:821-822)
GIVEN `separate branches of work that are commonly carried on as separate businesses in separate premises are carried on in separate departments on the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(5) each department is a separate factory or workshop` IS
    IF `separate branches of work that are commonly carried on as separate businesses in separate premises are carried on in separate departments on the same premises`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (1): "Subject to the regulations, if a claimant loses an employment, or is unable to resume an employment, because of a
-- work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant was
-- employed, the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits until the earlier of (a) the end of the work stoppage, and
-- (b) the day on which the claimant becomes regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment." Each "until" is a fact
-- about the day in question: has it happened by that day (fork ei2-F13). The premises are those of s 36(5) where it applies.
-- src:809 | Labour disputes
-- src:810 | 36 (1) Subject to the regulations, if a claimant loses an employment, or is unable to resume an employment, because of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant was employed, the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits until the earlier of
-- src:811 | (a) the end of the work stoppage, and
-- src:812 | (b) the day on which the claimant becomes regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 36(1) (src:809-812)
GIVEN `the claimant loses an employment, or is unable to resume an employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `because of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant was employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work stoppage has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has become regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(1) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits` IF
        `the claimant loses an employment, or is unable to resume an employment`
    AND `because of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant was employed`
    AND (NOT `the work stoppage has ended`)
    AND (NOT `the claimant has become regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment`)

-- (3): "A disentitlement under this section is suspended during any period for which the claimant (a) establishes that
-- the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits or benefits by virtue of section 25; and (b) establishes, in such
-- manner as the Commission may direct, that before the work stoppage, the claimant had anticipated being absent from their
-- employment because of any reason entitling them to those benefits and had begun making arrangements in relation to
-- the absence." Both (a) and (b) are for the claimant to establish.
-- src:815 | Suspension of disentitlement
-- src:816 | (3) A disentitlement under this section is suspended during any period for which the claimant
-- src:817 | (a) establishes that the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits or benefits by virtue of section 25; and
-- src:818 | (b) establishes, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that before the work stoppage, the claimant had anticipated being absent from their employment because of any reason entitling them to those benefits and had begun making arrangements in relation to the absence.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 36(3) (src:815-818)
GIVEN `the claimant establishes that the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the claimant establishes that the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits by virtue of section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant establishes that before the work stoppage the claimant had anticipated being absent from their employment because of a reason entitling them to those benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had begun making arrangements in relation to the absence before the work stoppage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(3) the disentitlement is suspended for the period` IF
        (   (`the claimant establishes that the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the period` AND `s 2(1) special benefits` `the reason for those benefits`)
         OR `the claimant establishes that the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits by virtue of section 25`)
    AND `the claimant establishes that before the work stoppage the claimant had anticipated being absent from their employment because of a reason entitling them to those benefits`
    AND `the claimant had begun making arrangements in relation to the absence before the work stoppage`

-- (4): "This section does not apply if a claimant proves that the claimant is not participating in, financing or directly
-- interested in the labour dispute that caused the stoppage of work." The claimant must prove all three negatives.
-- src:819 | Non-application
-- src:820 | (4) This section does not apply if a claimant proves that the claimant is not participating in, financing or directly interested in the labour dispute that caused the stoppage of work.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 36(4) (src:819-820)
GIVEN `the claimant proves that the claimant is not participating in the labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that the claimant is not financing the labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that the claimant is not directly interested in the labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(4) this section does not apply to the claimant` IF
        `the claimant proves that the claimant is not participating in the labour dispute`
    AND `the claimant proves that the claimant is not financing the labour dispute`
    AND `the claimant proves that the claimant is not directly interested in the labour dispute`

-- The section as a whole on a given day: the disentitlement of (1), unless suspended by (3) or the section does not apply by (4).
-- src:809 | Labour disputes
-- src:810 | 36 (1) Subject to the regulations, if a claimant loses an employment, or is unable to resume an employment, because of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which the claimant was employed, the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits until the earlier of
-- src:811 | (a) the end of the work stoppage, and
-- src:812 | (b) the day on which the claimant becomes regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment.
-- src:813 | Regulations
-- src:814 | (2) The Commission may, with the approval of the Governor in Council, make regulations for determining the number of days of disentitlement in a week of a claimant who loses a part-time employment or is unable to resume a part-time employment because of the reason mentioned in subsection (1).
-- src:815 | Suspension of disentitlement
-- src:816 | (3) A disentitlement under this section is suspended during any period for which the claimant
-- src:817 | (a) establishes that the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits or benefits by virtue of section 25; and
-- src:818 | (b) establishes, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that before the work stoppage, the claimant had anticipated being absent from their employment because of any reason entitling them to those benefits and had begun making arrangements in relation to the absence.
-- src:819 | Non-application
-- src:820 | (4) This section does not apply if a claimant proves that the claimant is not participating in, financing or directly interested in the labour dispute that caused the stoppage of work.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 36(1), s 36(3), s 36(4) (src:809-820)
GIVEN `the claimant is not entitled under subsection 36(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disentitlement is suspended under subsection 36(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 36 does not apply to the claimant under subsection 36(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36 the claimant is disentitled on the day` IF
        `the claimant is not entitled under subsection 36(1)`
    AND (NOT `the disentitlement is suspended under subsection 36(3)`)
    AND (NOT `section 36 does not apply to the claimant under subsection 36(4)`)

§ `Section 37 - prison inmates and persons outside Canada`

-- "Except as may otherwise be prescribed, a claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for any period during which the
-- claimant (a) is an inmate of a prison or similar institution; or (b) is not in Canada." What is otherwise prescribed is
-- regs 54 and 55 (out of range: piece er3): one BOOLEAN input, "an exception is prescribed for the claimant's case".
-- src:823 | Prison inmates and persons outside Canada
-- src:824 | 37 Except as may otherwise be prescribed, a claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for any period during which the claimant
-- src:825 | (a) is an inmate of a prison or similar institution; or
-- src:826 | (b) is not in Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 37 (src:823-826)
GIVEN `the claimant is an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is not in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception is prescribed that covers the claimant's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 37 the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for the period` IF
        (`the claimant is an inmate of a prison or similar institution` OR `the claimant is not in Canada`)
    AND (NOT `an exception is prescribed that covers the claimant's case`)
